syntax: a here-document is pending only once its word is parsed

A here-document redirect was added to the pending here-documents before
its word was parsed. When reading that word crossed a newline, as an
unclosed subscript does in "<<$A[\n" with zsh, the lexer read the
pending here-document bodies at that newline and dereferenced the word
that was still being parsed, which was nil, and panicked. The redirect
is now added once its word is complete.

Reproducer, before this change: parse "<<$A[\n" with LangZsh; it panics
in unquotedWordBytes.

